{"module":"policing","voice":"female","duration":252.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"La policía y la llamada al 911","start":0.0,"end":3.16,"words":[[0.11,0.28],[0.28,0.94],[0.94,1.02],[1.02,1.19],[1.19,1.68],[1.68,1.85],[1.85,3.09]]},{"el":"intro","text":"La Ley CAREN trata de un daño específico: llamar a la policía contra alguien por su raza.","start":3.96,"end":10.4,"words":[[4.07,4.22],[4.22,4.46],[4.46,4.85],[4.85,5.24],[5.24,5.39],[5.39,5.55],[5.55,5.86],[5.86,6.71],[6.99,7.38],[7.38,7.45],[7.45,7.61],[7.61,8.23],[8.23,8.7],[8.7,9.17],[9.17,9.4],[9.4,9.56],[9.56,9.94]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Este módulo muestra de dónde viene ese daño y por qué una llamada puede ser peligrosa.","start":10.75,"end":16.85,"words":[[10.84,11.16],[11.16,11.64],[11.64,12.21],[12.21,12.37],[12.37,12.77],[12.77,13.17],[13.17,13.41],[13.41,13.73],[13.73,13.81],[13.81,14.05],[14.05,14.21],[14.21,14.45],[14.45,14.93],[14.93,15.33],[15.33,15.57],[15.57,16.38]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Patrullas de esclavos","start":17.2,"end":18.66,"words":[[17.31,17.91],[17.91,18.04],[18.04,18.57]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Desde la ley de Carolina del Sur de 1704, las colonias y estados del Sur organizaron patrullas de esclavos: hombres blancos que recorrían de noche, detenían a personas negras, exigían pases, registraban las viviendas de los esclavizados y azotaban a quienes encontraban sin permiso.","start":19.36,"end":38.32,"words":[[19.47,19.81],[19.81,19.94],[19.94,20.15],[20.15,20.28],[20.28,20.82],[20.82,21.03],[21.03,21.23],[21.23,21.37],[21.37,22.79],[23.03,23.23],[23.23,23.77],[23.77,23.84],[23.84,24.31],[24.31,24.52],[24.52,24.72],[24.72,25.46],[25.46,26.07],[26.07,26.21],[26.21,26.82],[27.06,27.46],[27.46,27.94],[27.94,28.07],[28.07,28.68],[28.68,28.82],[28.82,29.22],[29.46,30.07],[30.07,30.14],[30.14,30.68],[30.68,31.15],[31.39,32.0],[32.0,32.41],[32.64,33.39],[33.39,33.59],[33.59,34.2],[34.2,34.34],[34.34,34.54],[34.54,35.35],[35.35,35.42],[35.42,35.96],[35.96,36.03],[36.03,36.44],[36.44,37.18],[37.18,37.39],[37.39,37.93]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Se esperaba que toda persona blanca ayudara a vigilar a los esclavizados.","start":38.67,"end":43.27,"words":[[38.73,38.86],[38.86,39.4],[39.4,39.53],[39.53,39.8],[39.8,40.27],[40.27,40.67],[40.67,41.13],[41.13,41.2],[41.2,41.67],[41.67,41.74],[41.74,41.94],[41.94,42.8]]},{"el":"h1","text":"De las patrullas a la policía","start":44.17,"end":46.19,"words":[[44.3,44.45],[44.45,44.67],[44.67,45.34],[45.34,45.42],[45.42,45.56],[45.56,46.16]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Tras la emancipación, muchas funciones de las patrullas del Sur pasaron a la nueva policía municipal y a los alguaciles.","start":46.89,"end":54.69,"words":[[46.97,47.24],[47.24,47.38],[47.38,48.28],[48.53,48.94],[48.94,49.57],[49.57,49.71],[49.71,49.91],[49.91,50.54],[50.54,50.75],[50.75,50.95],[50.95,51.44],[51.44,51.51],[51.51,51.65],[51.65,51.99],[51.99,52.55],[52.55,53.17],[53.17,53.24],[53.24,53.31],[53.31,53.52],[53.52,54.28]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Qué tan directa es la línea entre las patrullas y la policía moderna se debate: los departamentos del Norte (Boston 1838, Nueva York 1845) surgieron sobre todo del modelo de Londres y del control de inmigrantes y trabajadores.","start":55.04,"end":72.53,"words":[[55.11,55.25],[55.25,55.46],[55.46,55.94],[55.94,56.08],[56.08,56.22],[56.22,56.57],[56.57,56.92],[56.92,57.13],[57.13,57.76],[57.76,57.82],[57.82,57.96],[57.96,58.52],[58.52,59.01],[59.01,59.15],[59.15,59.64],[59.88,60.09],[60.09,60.99],[60.99,61.2],[61.2,61.55],[61.55,61.97],[61.97,63.92],[64.16,64.51],[64.51,64.79],[64.79,66.74],[66.99,67.61],[67.61,67.96],[67.96,68.24],[68.24,68.45],[68.45,68.87],[68.87,69.01],[69.01,69.49],[69.49,69.56],[69.56,69.77],[69.77,70.26],[70.26,70.4],[70.4,71.17],[71.17,71.23],[71.23,72.14]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los historiadores coinciden en que en el Sur la tarea de controlar el movimiento de las personas negras continuó.","start":72.88,"end":78.78,"words":[[72.97,73.15],[73.15,73.86],[73.86,74.39],[74.39,74.51],[74.51,74.62],[74.62,74.74],[74.74,74.86],[74.86,75.04],[75.04,75.16],[75.16,75.45],[75.45,75.57],[75.57,76.1],[76.1,76.22],[76.22,76.81],[76.81,76.92],[76.92,77.1],[77.1,77.57],[77.57,77.93],[77.93,78.46]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Códigos Negros, leyes de vagancia y arrendamiento de presos","start":79.68,"end":83.79,"words":[[79.78,80.3],[80.3,80.81],[81.07,81.44],[81.44,81.59],[81.59,82.18],[82.18,82.25],[82.25,83.13],[83.13,83.28],[83.28,83.72]]},{"el":"s2","text":"La Decimotercera Enmienda (1865) abolió la esclavitud “excepto como castigo por un delito”.","start":84.49,"end":91.89,"words":[[84.62,84.76],[84.76,85.64],[85.64,86.18],[86.18,88.01],[88.25,88.65],[88.65,88.79],[88.79,89.46],[89.46,89.94],[89.94,90.21],[90.21,90.68],[90.68,90.89],[90.89,91.02],[91.02,91.5]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los estados del Sur aprobaron de inmediato Códigos Negros que convertían en delito que las personas negras estuvieran desempleadas, caminaran de noche o “merodearan”.","start":92.24,"end":102.33,"words":[[92.38,92.58],[92.58,93.04],[93.04,93.24],[93.24,93.44],[93.44,94.05],[94.05,94.18],[94.18,94.78],[94.78,95.25],[95.25,95.65],[95.65,95.78],[95.78,96.51],[96.51,96.65],[96.65,97.05],[97.05,97.18],[97.18,97.38],[97.38,97.92],[97.92,98.32],[98.32,98.98],[98.98,99.85],[100.08,100.68],[100.68,100.82],[100.82,101.15],[101.15,101.22],[101.22,101.95]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Los arrestados eran arrendados a plantaciones, minas y ferrocarriles, y a menudo morían a tasas más altas que bajo la esclavitud.","start":102.68,"end":111.56,"words":[[102.78,103.0],[103.0,103.67],[103.67,103.97],[103.97,104.64],[104.64,104.72],[104.72,105.69],[105.95,106.32],[106.32,106.4],[106.4,107.29],[107.55,107.63],[107.63,107.7],[107.7,108.15],[108.15,108.67],[108.67,108.75],[108.75,109.12],[109.12,109.34],[109.34,109.72],[109.72,109.87],[109.87,110.16],[110.16,110.31],[110.31,111.13]]},{"el":"s2","text":"El arrendamiento de presos duró en Alabama hasta 1928.","start":111.91,"end":116.32,"words":[[112.03,112.15],[112.15,112.88],[112.88,113.0],[113.0,113.36],[113.36,113.61],[113.61,113.73],[113.73,114.15],[114.15,114.4],[114.4,115.97]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Una acusación podía ser una sentencia de muerte","start":117.22,"end":120.85,"words":[[117.29,117.55],[117.55,118.32],[118.32,118.83],[118.83,119.09],[119.09,119.35],[119.35,120.12],[120.12,120.29],[120.29,120.8]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Muchos linchamientos empezaron con una acusación de una persona blanca.","start":121.55,"end":126.58,"words":[[121.61,122.05],[122.05,123.0],[123.0,123.65],[123.65,123.87],[123.87,124.09],[124.09,124.75],[124.75,124.89],[124.89,125.11],[125.11,125.62],[125.62,126.13]]},{"el":"s3","text":"En 1955, el relato de Carolyn Bryant sobre un encuentro en una tienda de Misisipi llevó al asesinato de Emmett Till, de 14 años.","start":126.93,"end":136.79,"words":[[127.01,127.14],[127.14,129.14],[129.37,129.51],[129.51,129.91],[129.91,130.04],[130.04,130.51],[130.51,130.97],[130.97,131.3],[131.3,131.44],[131.44,132.04],[132.04,132.17],[132.17,132.37],[132.37,132.77],[132.77,132.9],[132.9,133.43],[133.43,133.7],[133.7,133.83],[133.83,134.43],[134.43,134.57],[134.57,134.97],[134.97,135.23],[135.46,135.6],[135.6,136.06],[136.06,136.4]]},{"el":"s3","text":"(En un libro de 2017, el historiador Timothy Tyson informó que ella admitió después que partes de su relato no eran ciertas; su familia lo niega.","start":137.14,"end":147.36,"words":[[137.23,137.37],[137.37,137.52],[137.52,137.88],[137.88,138.03],[138.03,139.26],[139.51,139.66],[139.66,140.38],[140.38,140.82],[140.82,141.18],[141.18,141.69],[141.69,141.83],[141.83,142.12],[142.12,142.63],[142.63,143.14],[143.14,143.28],[143.28,143.72],[143.72,143.86],[143.86,144.01],[144.01,144.44],[144.44,144.59],[144.59,144.88],[144.88,145.46],[145.71,145.86],[145.86,146.36],[146.36,146.51],[146.51,146.94]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Ese detalle está debatido.)","start":147.71,"end":149.55,"words":[[147.78,147.98],[147.98,148.44],[148.44,148.7],[148.7,149.28]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La lección en la que se basa la Ley CAREN es más antigua que cualquier caso: cuando la persona denunciada es negra, la respuesta policial puede ser mortal.","start":149.9,"end":159.83,"words":[[150.0,150.14],[150.14,150.64],[150.64,150.79],[150.79,150.93],[150.93,151.07],[151.07,151.21],[151.21,151.5],[151.5,151.64],[151.64,151.85],[151.85,152.21],[152.21,152.35],[152.35,152.57],[152.57,153.07],[153.07,153.21],[153.21,153.78],[153.78,154.14],[154.39,154.81],[154.81,154.96],[154.96,155.46],[155.46,156.17],[156.17,156.31],[156.31,156.74],[156.99,157.13],[157.13,157.77],[157.77,158.34],[158.34,158.7],[158.7,158.91],[158.91,159.41]]},{"el":"h4","text":"La llamada al 911 usada como arma hoy","start":160.73,"end":164.23,"words":[[160.82,160.99],[160.99,161.49],[161.49,161.66],[161.66,162.93],[162.93,163.35],[163.35,163.68],[163.68,164.02],[164.02,164.19]]},{"el":"s4","text":"En 2018 y 2020, videos mostraron a personas blancas llamando a la policía contra personas negras que hacían una barbacoa (Oakland), esperaban en un Starbucks (Filadelfia, donde arrestaron a dos hombres), vendían agua (San Francisco) y observaban aves (Central Park).","start":164.93,"end":184.84,"words":[[165.01,165.17],[165.17,166.39],[166.39,166.47],[166.47,167.46],[167.73,168.19],[168.19,168.88],[168.88,168.95],[168.95,169.57],[169.57,170.1],[170.1,170.64],[170.64,170.71],[170.71,170.87],[170.87,171.48],[171.48,171.94],[171.94,172.55],[172.55,173.01],[173.01,173.16],[173.16,173.62],[173.62,173.85],[173.85,174.46],[174.46,175.07],[175.34,176.03],[176.03,176.18],[176.18,176.34],[176.34,176.95],[176.95,177.79],[178.06,178.44],[178.44,179.13],[179.13,179.2],[179.2,179.43],[179.43,179.97],[180.24,180.85],[180.85,181.15],[181.15,181.38],[181.38,182.07],[182.34,182.42],[182.42,183.18],[183.18,183.49],[183.49,184.02],[184.02,184.41]]},{"el":"s4","text":"San Francisco aprobó la Ley CAREN en 2020, después de la ley de Oregón de 2019 y la AB 1775 de California.","start":185.19,"end":195.09,"words":[[185.28,185.5],[185.5,186.14],[186.14,186.57],[186.57,186.71],[186.71,186.93],[186.93,187.28],[187.28,187.43],[187.43,188.36],[188.61,189.11],[189.11,189.25],[189.25,189.39],[189.39,189.61],[189.61,189.75],[189.75,190.18],[190.18,190.32],[190.32,191.46],[191.46,191.53],[191.53,191.68],[191.68,191.82],[191.82,193.75],[193.75,193.89],[193.89,194.68]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Los datos respaldan los videos.","start":195.44,"end":197.61,"words":[[195.56,195.73],[195.73,196.03],[196.03,196.56],[196.56,196.73],[196.73,197.15]]},{"el":"s4","text":"En San Francisco, solo alrededor del 1% de las llamadas por “persona sospechosa” del último año terminó en arresto, multa o informe.","start":197.96,"end":207.16,"words":[[198.06,198.2],[198.2,198.41],[198.41,199.11],[199.36,199.64],[199.64,200.27],[200.27,200.48],[200.48,201.32],[201.32,201.46],[201.46,201.67],[201.67,202.16],[202.16,202.37],[202.37,202.86],[202.86,203.56],[203.56,203.77],[203.77,204.2],[204.2,204.41],[204.41,204.9],[204.9,205.04],[205.04,205.53],[205.77,206.12],[206.12,206.19],[206.19,206.76]]},{"el":"s4","text":"La Encuesta federal de Contacto entre la Policía y el Público (2020) halló que las personas negras que tuvieron contacto con la policía tenían casi tres veces más probabilidades que las blancas de sufrir amenazas o uso de la fuerza.","start":207.51,"end":221.84,"words":[[207.57,207.71],[207.71,208.26],[208.26,208.74],[208.74,208.88],[208.88,209.43],[209.43,209.78],[209.78,209.91],[209.91,210.46],[210.46,210.53],[210.53,210.67],[210.67,211.15],[211.15,211.98],[212.22,212.49],[212.49,212.63],[212.63,212.84],[212.84,213.39],[213.39,213.8],[213.8,213.94],[213.94,214.49],[214.49,215.04],[215.04,215.25],[215.25,215.38],[215.38,215.93],[215.93,216.42],[216.42,216.69],[216.69,216.97],[216.97,217.31],[217.31,217.52],[217.52,218.48],[218.48,218.62],[218.62,218.82],[218.82,219.31],[219.31,219.44],[219.44,219.86],[219.86,220.41],[220.41,220.47],[220.47,220.68],[220.68,220.82],[220.82,220.96],[220.96,221.44]]},{"el":"h5","text":"Lo que funciona","start":222.74,"end":223.8,"words":[[222.82,222.98],[222.98,223.13],[223.13,223.75]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Las ciudades están enviando equipos capacitados en lugar de policías armados a muchas llamadas.","start":224.5,"end":230.72,"words":[[224.62,224.83],[224.83,225.39],[225.39,225.74],[225.74,226.3],[226.3,226.73],[226.73,227.5],[227.5,227.64],[227.64,227.99],[227.99,228.13],[228.13,228.77],[228.77,229.26],[229.26,229.33],[229.33,229.75],[229.75,230.31]]},{"el":"s5","text":"El programa CAHOOTS de Eugene, Oregón, lo hace desde 1989.","start":231.07,"end":236.43,"words":[[231.15,231.28],[231.28,231.79],[231.79,232.17],[232.17,232.3],[232.3,232.74],[232.96,233.41],[233.63,233.76],[233.76,233.95],[233.95,234.27],[234.27,236.05]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Un estudio de 2022 en Science Advances halló que el programa STAR de Denver redujo las denuncias de los delitos menores que atendía.","start":236.78,"end":244.97,"words":[[236.86,236.99],[236.99,237.45],[237.45,237.58],[237.58,238.56],[238.56,238.69],[238.69,239.08],[239.08,239.61],[239.61,239.87],[239.87,240.0],[240.0,240.13],[240.13,240.65],[240.65,240.91],[240.91,241.04],[241.04,241.44],[241.44,241.83],[241.83,242.02],[242.02,242.61],[242.61,242.74],[242.74,242.94],[242.94,243.39],[243.39,243.85],[243.85,243.98],[243.98,244.57]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Una Ley CAREN federal añade la otra mitad: una consecuencia por usar a la policía como arma.","start":245.32,"end":251.29,"words":[[245.39,245.59],[245.59,245.8],[245.8,246.14],[246.14,246.62],[246.62,246.96],[246.96,247.1],[247.1,247.37],[247.37,247.78],[248.02,248.23],[248.23,249.05],[249.05,249.25],[249.25,249.53],[249.53,249.59],[249.59,249.73],[249.73,250.28],[250.28,250.55],[250.55,250.89]]}]}